sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis22-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis22-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis22-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Holaspis22 cuticle Turing wavelength at 15 µm (Wenlock, 428.1 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 79.9/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Schnakenberg reaction-diffusion on a periodic cuticle patch, with D_u and D_v chosen so the analytical critical wavelength is 15.14 µm. Dispersion check on exact Fourier modes gives Pearson r = 0.99963 (RMSE 0.03185). Equal-diffusivity control amplitude ratio is 0.036. Versus holaspis18, four extra meraspid Dyar steps (ratio 1.115) enlarge entry length by 1.546, so each t22 tergite holds 1.265 times as many 15 µm tiles. The pinned fossil's post-cephalic rib field measures 23.89 rings against the literature thoracic count of 22. Overall 79.9/100 (faithfulness 77.7, reproducibility 84.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8b3e13105b55d8ac28c3f835f3a5a27bb4faff45; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 1.26.4, scipy 1.18.1, pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 62, Morphometric validation 76, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis22_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis22-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 8b3e13105b55d8ac28c3f835f3a5a27bb4faff45, image/gif, 3951972 B, 611×720 px, 14 frames, artifact_sha256 3284ad707b7efd78aef2da088279abd602641ebc3eea61d6ee0352cf80da551d (sha256 3284ad707b7efd78aef2da088279abd602641ebc3eea61d6ee0352cf80da551d), spec_fingerprint 47904938ec440c71d3ae9e4ad06d8226684eebc47ce74d3df60816aaa69afd77. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 47904938ec440c71d3ae9e4ad06d8226684eebc47ce74d3df60816aaa69afd77; artifact_sha256: 3284ad707b7efd78aef2da088279abd602641ebc3eea61d6ee0352cf80da551d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis22_turing_wavelength_s0/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis22_specimen.jpg=1b6c8997dc42e91d..., datasets/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis22_turing_wavelength_s0/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis22_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=27a4d89f420f5947..., datasets/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis22_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=18715738c9f9b9cc..., datasets/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis22_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=05678f16da15a24f...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Five holaspid morphs with 18–22 thoracic segments; hemianamorphosis; precocious specification of the adult count (Fusco et al. 2004). | Meraspid per-stage growth 1.115 and holaspid per-stage growth 1.103; thoracic release ends at s18 for t18 and s22 for t22 (Hughes et al. 2017). | A shape transition near glabellar length 1.7 mm is not strictly tied to segment number (Hughes & Chapman 1995).; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg Jacobian and k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v), with the length unit set so lambda_c = 1.514e-5 m. | Entry-size ratio 1.115^4 and the per-tergite wavelength-count ratio against the 18-segment predecessor. | Segment-accretion reveal on the pinned dorsal photograph, with the simulated activator painted into the two eye regions.; transfer_boundary: The catalog ages 428.3 Ma (holaspis18) and 428.1 Ma (holaspis22) are series bookkeeping. Fusco et al. 2004 describe contemporaneous intraspecific morphs from one narrow Wenlock interval near 429 Ma. | 15 µm is the assigned cellular detail scale for this slot. It is not a lens diameter measured on Aulacopleura.; does_not_claim: That the fossil photograph resolves 15 µm ocelli. | That 18- and 22-segment animals are successive chronospecies separated by 0.2 Myr. | That Schnakenberg kinetics were written down by Fusco, Hughes, or Turing; Turing 1952 supplies the dispersion relation, Schnakenberg supplies a two-species carrier that realizes it.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R1: Sweep diffusivity ratio r = D_v/D_u at fixed D_u and show that lambda_c increases monotonically.",
            "remediation needed: R2: Add a quadratic-term ablation (drop u^2 v) beside the equal-diffusion negative control.",
            "remediation needed: R3: Segment the specimen and the GIF last frame with the 12-bin Sobel orientation histogram and the 24-bin radial FFT used by verify_image_fitness, and report a KS statistic.",
            "remediation needed: R4: Put Pearson r, RMSE, and the new KS/CV terms on the comparison figure." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.799"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

